subtitle: what did we expect?

Expectedly, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has resoundingly rejected the proposed school bill, viewing it as an affront to their ideals of the separation of church and state. With little room for compromise, we have decided to collapse the Fourth Marx Cabinet. However, in accordance with Hindenburg’s wishes, the coalition will pass the budget for the upcoming year before the upcoming elections. 

While Marx IV has achieved legislative successes in the area of social policy, labor-management relations have deteriorated sharply and class antagonisms have flared up within the party. Marx, as Chairman of the Catholic Schools Association, has faced much rebuke from the rank-and-file due to the failure of the law. He will resign at the upcoming party congress in December. Meanwhile, in light of the formation of the <span style="color: #909090;">**CSRP**</span> and the growing appeal of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>, the outlook for the upcoming election in May looks increasingly bleak. 

@accept
